From 0296f744bf5843320585b4c57a93dcb64bdab79b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mick <sirmick@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 09:29:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Unicorn PPC: map memory, open engine, run 1000 insns at
 nanokernel entry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Milestone 1 of docs/ppc/UnicornPpcPlan.md: the backend opens Unicorn,
mirrors KPX's memory map byte-for-byte, sets initial CPU state
(PC=ROM+0x310000, GPR3=ROM+0x30d000, GPR4=KD+0x1000, MODE_68K),
and runs until a configurable instruction count or event.

Changes:
- cpu_unicorn_ppc.cpp: REAL_ADDRESSING memory accessors (usable by
  InitAll_PPC immediately), uc_open with PPC32+BIG_ENDIAN, CPU model
  PPC32_750_V3_1 (matches KPX PVR 0x000c0000), uc_mem_map_ptr for
  RAM+NKpad / ROM / KD aliases / DR probe regions, PC/GPR setup,
  register read/write wrappers, minimal execute loop with 1000-insn
  cap.
- subprojects/unicorn/uc.c: drop the NULL-pointer guard in
  uc_mem_map_ptr — REAL_ADDRESSING legitimately mmaps RAM at host
  address 0 (MAP_FIXED at 0 with vm.mmap_min_addr=0), which the
  guard was rejecting.

Still stubbed (next increments): EmulOp dispatch via major opcode 6
(needs translate.c patch), IRQ injection handshake, PPC→68k execute
bridge, tick thread.

Verified: `--arch ppc --backend unicorn` runs 1000 insns from
0x50310000 with UC_ERR_OK; `--arch m68k --backend unicorn` still
boots to Finder in 11.47s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 uc.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/uc.c b/uc.c
index 75b89a0..dbe106d 100644
--- a/uc.c
+++ b/uc.c
@@ -1413,10 +1413,11 @@ uc_err uc_mem_map_ptr(uc_engine *uc, uint64_t address, uint64_t size,
 
     UC_INIT(uc);
 
-    if (ptr == NULL) {
-        restore_jit_state(uc);
-        return UC_ERR_ARG;
-    }
+    // The NULL-pointer check was a sanity guard, but REAL_ADDRESSING guests
+    // (e.g., mac-phoenix's PPC layout) legitimately mmap RAM at host address 0
+    // via MAP_FIXED, making RAMBaseHost == NULL. The kernel-facing store only
+    // dereferences the pointer via offset arithmetic, so page 0 is fine as
+    // long as the caller has actually mapped it.
 
     res = mem_map_check(uc, address, size, perms);
     if (res) {
